        "sid": "2KI 24"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "24",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In his days Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up, and Jehoiakim became his servant three years; then he turned and rebelled against him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " sent against him bands of the Chaldeans, and bands of the Syrians, and bands of the Moabites, and bands of the Ammonites, and sent them against Judah to destroy it, according to the word of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " which he spoke by his servants the prophets. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Surely this came upon Judah at the command of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", to remove them out of his sight, for the sins of Manasseh, according to all that he had done, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and also for the innocent blood that he had shed; for he filled Jerusalem with innocent blood, and the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " would not pardon. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now the rest of the deeds of Jehoiakim, and all that he did, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So Jehoiakim slept with his fathers, and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his stead. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the king of Egypt did not come again out of his land, for the king of Babylon had taken all that belonged to the king of Egypt from the Brook of Egypt to the river Euphrates.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.7"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2CH.36.9+2CH.36.10"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Chron 36.9-10",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he became king, and he reigned three months in Jerusalem. His mother's name was Nehushta the daughter of Elnathan of Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he did what was evil in the sight of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", according to all that his father had done.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "At that time the servants of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up to Jerusalem, and the city was besieged. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to the city, while his servants were besieging it; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and Jehoiachin the king of Judah gave himself up to the king of Babylon, himself, and his mother, and his servants, and his princes, and his palace officials. The king of Babylon took him prisoner in the eighth year of his reign, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and carried off all the treasures of the house of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", and the treasures of the king's house, and cut in pieces all the vessels of gold in the temple of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", which Solomon king of Israel had made, as the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " had foretold. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He carried away all Jerusalem, and all the princes, and all the mighty men of valor, ten thousand captives, and all the craftsmen and the smiths; none remained, except the poorest people of the land. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he carried away Jehoiachin to Babylon; the king's mother, the king's wives, his officials, and the chief men of the land, he took into captivity from Jerusalem to Babylon. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the king of Babylon brought captive to Babylon all the men of valor, seven thousand, and the craftsmen and the smiths, one thousand, all of them strong and fit for war. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 24:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the king of Babylon made Mattaniah, Jehoiachin's uncle, king in his stead, and changed his name to Zedekiah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.24.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.24.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
